CASE = [
 Q("<b>Case study.</b> Meera lives in a city of 15 lakh people. Her ward has an overflowing garbage dump, and the street light on her lane has not worked for a month. She writes to her ward councillor, who raises the matter in the city's governing body. The dump is cleared within a week. "
   "(i) Which urban local body governs a city of 15 lakh people? (ii) Who is the elected head of this body? (iii) Name one service mentioned in the passage. (iv) What does Meera's action show about the role of citizens in local democracy?",
   "(i) Municipal Corporation (1). (ii) The Mayor (1). (iii) Garbage collection or street lighting (1). (iv) Citizens should report problems to their representatives (1); active participation helps the body respond to local needs (1).", "1+1+1+2"),
 Q("<b>Case study.</b> A small town in Kerala has about 40,000 residents. Its Municipal Council collects property tax and fees, and uses the money to repair roads and supply drinking water. Residents are asked to separate wet and dry waste at home so that collection becomes easier. "
   "(i) Which body governs a town of 40,000 people? (ii) Give another name for this body. (iii) Name one source of its income. (iv) Why does waste segregation by citizens help the local body?",
   "(i) Municipal Council (1). (ii) Nagar Palika (1). (iii) Property tax or fees (1). (iv) Separated waste is easier and quicker to collect and process (1); it saves the body's money and keeps the town cleaner, showing shared responsibility (1).", "1+1+1+2"),
 Q("<b>Case study.</b> A growing village near Pune begins to develop shops, small factories and new housing. The authorities declare it a transitional area between rural and urban and set up a Nagar Panchayat. Its elected members now plan drains, roads and water supply for the area. "
   "(i) Which urban local body was set up here? (ii) Why is the area called a transitional area? (iii) Name one work the Nagar Panchayat will plan. (iv) Why is it useful to have different types of bodies for different-sized settlements?",
   "(i) Nagar Panchayat (1). (ii) It is changing from a rural area into an urban one (1). (iii) Drains, roads or water supply (1). (iv) Needs of a small town differ from those of a big city (1); a suitable body can manage them with the right level of power and resources (1).", "1+1+1+2"),
]

